-- Synthetic sandbox journal corpus for the isolated testing database.
--
-- WHAT: ~120 realistic Entries spread across the last ~61 days, written to
-- replace the 19th-century literary-diary test corpus with something that
-- actually reads like a modern journal app's real content: casual, mundane,
-- specific, mostly short. Seven recurring threads (a knee injury and its
-- physio arc, a work migration codenamed 'Aurora' with a colleague Devika,
-- a friend Priya's wedding, a caffeine/sleep experiment, a couple of books,
-- a flat move, and a parent's health check-up) interleave with one-off
-- entries, the way a real journal is mostly noise with a few threads running
-- through it. Two entry bodies are literal search terms ('knee' and 'flat
-- move?') that apps/web/src/lib/sessions-transport.test.ts already exercises.
--
-- WHY RELATIVE DATES: every created_at below is computed as an offset from
-- now() (`date_trunc('day', now()) - interval 'N days' + interval 'H hours
-- M minutes'`) rather than a pinned calendar date. The Digest feature (ADR
-- 0027) builds day/week/month Periods around the current date, so a corpus
-- pinned to a fixed date would silently go stale — 'the last two months'
-- would eventually mean nothing. Reseeding this file always produces a
-- corpus that is, relative to whenever it's run, the last two months.
--
-- WHY embedding/embedding_model ARE NULL: per ADR 0022, embeddings are
-- filled by a background worker (server/src/embedding.rs) that scans for
-- `embedding is null` and embeds every Entry off the request path. Seeding
-- a value here would fight that worker and could easily be wrong for
-- whatever embedding model is actually configured; leaving it NULL lets the
-- real worker do its real job against this corpus, same as any other Entry.
--
-- WHY A FEW deleted_at ROWS: two are included as tombstones so the delete
-- path (migration 0005) has real data to exercise. Matching real client
-- behaviour on delete (see that migration's comment), their `body` is the
-- blank string a client sends alongside a delete, not the original text.
--
-- Every row is fixed to a literal uuid and this insert ends with `ON
-- CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING`, so re-running this file (e.g. from
-- scripts/seed-sandbox.sh) is idempotent — it never duplicates rows, only
-- the ages of the relative dates above will have shifted with the clock.
--
-- This is entirely synthetic content, written for this repository's testing
-- purposes. It is not scraped or adapted from any real person's diary.
--
-- Voice/register modelled loosely on everyday-diary sites like deardiary.net:
-- first person, mundane, specific, unpolished, not literary.

-- Single shared device_id for this corpus, as if written from one Device.
-- (fixed literal: 5593fa97-b8d8-4a33-a4ce-b967e9b63bfe)

insert into entries (id, device_id, body, created_at, deleted_at) values
  ('763f3f35-a3a7-471a-88d6-b51bd81f12eb', '5593fa97-b8d8-4a33-a4ce-b967e9b63bfe', $$Kickoff call for Aurora this morning. That's the codename they've landed on for the
database migration project — moving us off the old sharded setup onto something
that (allegedly) won't page me at 3am anymore. Devika's leading it, which is good,
she's sharp and doesn't sugarcoat timelines. First milestone pencilled in for
six weeks out. We'll see.$$, date_trunc('day', now()) - interval '61 days' + interval '9 hours 15 minutes', NULL),
  ('8c1a840a-a8f5-45ac-b203-ff47f9b05580', '5593fa97-b8d8-4a33-a4ce-b967e9b63bfe', $$Ran at lunch, felt a weird twinge behind my kneecap on the last half mile. Probably nothing, ignored it, ate a sandwich at my desk like an animal.$$, date_trunc('day', now()) - interval '61 days' + interval '13 hours 40 minutes', NULL),
  ('9543684e-7dc6-428f-8c5b-e836574ef348', '5593fa97-b8d8-4a33-a4ce-b967e9b63bfe', $$Rain all day, the good kind, the kind you can hear on the window. Made pasta, watched half an episode of something and fell asleep on the sofa. Back hurts from that now too. Getting old is just a slow accumulation of small complaints.$$, date_trunc('day', now()) - interval '61 days' + interval '22 hours 50 minutes', NULL),
  ('25b09eea-db83-4471-96f0-834b41a91750', '5593fa97-b8d8-4a33-a4ce-b967e9b63bfe', $$Started Piranesi tonight, the one Priya's been telling me to read for about a year.
